    "summary": "No new work claimed: about three minutes of the run's budget remain, all questions in the record are answered or explicitly bounded, there are no open necessary gaps and no tractable lead left within the interval, so I am not manufacturing a marginal item or a duplicate revision. The path returned is the last accepted draft, unchanged, which the contract records as no_change.\n\nFor the offline reviewer, the run's essential outcome, all receipt-backed or source-cited:\n\nConfirmed defects — (1) a leadership-transfer order is accepted with no authority binding: the message carries no term and the receiver never inspects sender identity, term or membership, while the order itself suppresses both pre-vote and the known-leader vote rejection, so one order from a non-member claimed sender deposed a serving leader against an otherwise unchanged stale-term RequestVote control; (2) `GetConfiguration().Index()` is constant zero, and since the `prevIndex` guard only fires for non-zero values a change guarded with the value the API returned is applied after an intervening change while the genuine-index control is rejected; (3) a node recovered through InstallSnapshot keeps its log store index below the snapshot index, making `shouldSnapshot`'s unsigned delta permanently true, so the node rewrites an identical full-state snapshot every SnapshotInterval while idle (15 and 13 distinct snapshot IDs at one index across two executions, versus 1 for the leader control).\n\nConditional finding — a below-protocol-2 leader writes membership changes in the deprecated voter-only peer format, and the constructor restores versioned configurations regardless of the protocol version it runs, so a rollback-style restart can silently drop non-voting members; quorum cannot be lost and the library neither prevents nor warns about the rollback.\n\nNegative results with stated limits — snapshot recency enforced only by term (control-backed, no applied-index regression observed), a stranded leader's `VerifyLeader` completing with an error in the order of the leader lease, `ReloadConfig` rejecting a constructor-invalid merge without changing anything, configuration propagation converging in 25 of 25 rounds with no stale published membership while the entry was held, pipelined replication's optimistic cursor never becoming acknowledged state, the heartbeat fast path's lock-protected mutation set, and the documented contracts for log-store gaps, barriers, progress accessors, shutdown ordering, observation delivery, batching apply, RPC version admission and existing-state detection. Unresolved boundaries are recorded rather than smoothed over: the un-reproduced local failure of the captured upgrade test, and the heartbeat fast path being unexecutable in this run's isolation because no network namespace is available."
